        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3530016c-f344-5172-919d-69978a5b3702",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands and music acts: Daisy Chainsaw, Generationals\n- People: KatieJane Garside, Ted Joyner, Grant Widmer\n- Places: England, New Orleans, Louisiana\n- Roles: lead vocalist, lyricist\n- Products: Eleventeen, Con Law\n- Topics: alternative rock, new wave\n\nFacts:\n- Daisy Chainsaw were an English alternative rock band active from 1989 to 1995.\n- Generationals are an American new wave duo formed in New Orleans, Louisiana.\n- Daisy Chainsaw originally featured KatieJane Garside as lead vocalist and lyricist on the band's early EPs and on the debut album Eleventeen, which was released in 1992.\n- KatieJane Garside departed from Daisy Chainsaw in 1993.\n- Generationals consist of Ted Joyner and Grant Widmer.\n- Generationals released their debut album Con Law in July 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
